Lab patch for xray-rust v0.9.0 (30928ad51b4a434546cf143f8e385a8746523172), applied by
lab/footprint/rust-core-build.sh when XRS_PATCHES names this file. Never part of the pin.

The XHTTP H2 connection receive window is a constant at v0.9.0
(crates/xray-transport/src/stream/xhttp/config.rs:17, read at stream/xhttp/h2.rs:46 and
passed to h2's Builder::initial_connection_window_size at h2.rs:332); no JSON field sets it.
16 MiB per connection, and xmux opens up to 3 connections by default
(xray-config/src/model.rs:1135). This makes it 4 MiB: the unread DATA a connection may
hold, whatever its streams' windows (the mobile profile's 1 MiB growing to 4 MiB).

--- a/crates/xray-transport/src/stream/xhttp/config.rs
+++ b/crates/xray-transport/src/stream/xhttp/config.rs
@@ -14,7 +14,10 @@
 use super::super::http_headers::HeaderMap;
 
 pub(crate) const DEFAULT_H2_STREAM_RECEIVE_WINDOW: u32 = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
-pub(crate) const H2_CONNECTION_RECEIVE_WINDOW: u32 = 16 * 1024 * 1024;
+// ghostlane lab patch (h2-connection-window-4mib): 16 MiB -> 4 MiB, so the
+// unread DATA one XHTTP H2 connection may hold is 4 MiB however many streams
+// it carries. Stream windows above it are refused by h2_stream_receive_window.
+pub(crate) const H2_CONNECTION_RECEIVE_WINDOW: u32 = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
 
 pub(crate) fn h2_stream_receive_window(configured: Option<u32>) -> Result<u32, XhttpConfigError> {
     let value = configured.unwrap_or(DEFAULT_H2_STREAM_RECEIVE_WINDOW);
